<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Channels are chat rooms where multiple users can talk. Channel names begin with"
  )} <strong>#</strong>.
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Everyone in a channel sees the same conversation. A channel usually has a theme, a topic shown at the top, and a few people who look after it."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_join}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Joining a Channel")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_channels", "/join #channel-name")}</pre>
<pre>/join #elixir         {dgettext("help_channels", "Join a public channel")}
/join #secret mykey  {dgettext("help_channels", "Join a channel that has a key")}</pre>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "If the channel does not exist yet, joining creates it. The first person in a new channel becomes its owner and can set its modes."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_remove}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Leaving a Channel")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_channels", "/part [#channel-name]")}</pre>
<p>{dgettext("help_channels", "If no channel is specified, you leave the current channel.")}</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "You can add a short goodbye after the channel name. Everyone in the channel sees it."
  )}
</p>
<pre>/part #elixir Goodbye!</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_dialog_channel_list}>
  {dgettext("help_channels", "Listing Channels")}
</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_channels", "/list")}</pre>
<p>
  {dgettext("help_channels", "Or use the")}
  <strong>{dgettext("help_channels", "Channel List")}</strong> {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "button in the toolbar. Invite-only (+i) channels are marked with a +i badge; select one and choose Request Access... to send a knock request to its operators."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "Secret channels are not listed for people outside them. Private channels are listed without their name."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Rules and limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "A channel name starts with # and has no spaces. It can be up to 50 characters long."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "You can be in a limited number of channels at once. The default is 10, and the server administrator can change it."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "A channel can refuse you because of a ban, a key, a user limit, invite-only mode or registered-only mode."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "An unregistered channel closes when the last person leaves, and its topic and modes are lost. Register it with ChanServ to keep it, its settings and its access list."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_channels", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-join">{dgettext("help_channels", "Join Command")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-part">{dgettext("help_channels", "Part Command")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-list">{dgettext("help_channels", "Channel List")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-knock">{dgettext("help_channels", "Knock Command")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-modes-overview">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Modes")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="chanserv-register">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Registering a Channel")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-permissions">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Permissions")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
